---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

// Update this page, and the date, whenever the site adds a tracker, an
// affiliate programme, an embed or a form.
const UPDATED = "23 September 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy and affiliate links"
  description="What London Travel Geek collects, the cookies it uses, how to turn analytics off, and which affiliate programmes pay for the site."
>
  <article class="legal container">
    <p class="eyebrow">London Travel Geek</p>
    <h1>Privacy and affiliate links</h1>
    <p class="legal__intro">
      London Travel Geek is an independent site. Questions about this page or
      your data: <a href="mailto:robert@promptlybuilt.co.uk">robert@promptlybuilt.co.uk</a>.
      Last updated {UPDATED}.
    </p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p>
      There are no accounts, comments, newsletters or forms, so we never ask
      for your name or email address.
    </p>
    <p>
      We use <strong>Google Analytics</strong> to count visits: which pages are
      read, how people arrive, the device and browser, the town or country
      (from your IP address, which Google does not store), what is searched on
      the site, and which links are clicked, including affiliate links. It
      sets two cookies, <code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_YDK7Q2D8E8</code>, which
      last up to two years. Google signals and ad personalisation are switched
      off, so none of it is used for advertising.
    </p>

    <h2 id="analytics">Turning analytics off</h2>
    <p>
      Analytics never loads if your browser sends Global Privacy Control. Or
      use this button, which stops it on this browser:
    </p>
    <p class="legal__switch">
      <button type="button" id="analytics-toggle" class="legal__button">Turn analytics off</button>
      <span id="analytics-state" role="status"></span>
    </p>
    <p>You can also block or delete cookies in your browser's settings.</p>

    <h2 id="affiliate-links">Affiliate links</h2>
    <p>
      Links marked <strong>ad</strong> are affiliate links. If you book or buy
      through one, the company pays us a commission, and the price you pay is
      the same. Rankings and recommendations are never paid for: the
      <a href="/how-we-rank/">how we rank</a> page explains how guides are
      built.
    </p>
    <p>We are paid by:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Hotels.com</strong>, through CJ Affiliate, for hotel links</li>
      <li><strong>GetYourGuide</strong>, for tours, tickets and the activity widgets</li>
      <li><strong>London Box Office</strong>, through Awin, for theatre tickets</li>
      <li><strong>Skiddle</strong>, for festival and gig tickets</li>
      <li><strong>Nomad</strong> (through Impact), <strong>Saily</strong> and <strong>Klook</strong>, for eSIMs</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      When you follow an affiliate link, the company or network sets a cookie
      on its own site so the sale can be credited to us. Their privacy policies
      cover that. We add the name of the page the link was on, so we can see
      which guides earn; nothing about you is passed on.
    </p>

    <h2>Things other companies load</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>GetYourGuide</strong> activity widgets load from
        GetYourGuide's servers and are covered by its privacy policy.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Maps</strong> load map images from OpenStreetMap and the map
        code from unpkg.com, which receive your IP address.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>YouTube</strong> videos use YouTube's privacy-enhanced player and
        load nothing from YouTube until you press play.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Event listings on <a href="/whats-on/">What's On</a> come from venues' own
      box offices, Ticketmaster and DICE. Following a ticket link takes you to
      their site, where their privacy policies apply.
    </p>

    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>
      The site is hosted by <strong>Vercel</strong>, which processes standard
      request logs, including IP addresses, to serve and protect the site.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Under UK data protection law you can ask what data is held about you and
      object to its use: email
      <a href="mailto:robert@promptlybuilt.co.uk">robert@promptlybuilt.co.uk</a>.
      Most of what the site collects is held by Google; turning analytics off
      above stops any more being collected. If you are unhappy with how your
      data is handled, you can complain to the
      <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/">Information Commissioner's Office</a>.
    </p>

    <p><a href="/">Return to the London Travel Geek homepage</a></p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<script is:inline>
  (function () {
    var button = document.getElementById("analytics-toggle");
    var state = document.getElementById("analytics-state");
    function read() {
      try { return localStorage.getItem("ltg-analytics") === "off"; } catch (e) { return false; }
    }
    function show() {
      var off = read() || navigator.globalPrivacyControl === true;
      button.textContent = off ? "Turn analytics back on" : "Turn analytics off";
      button.hidden = navigator.globalPrivacyControl === true;
      state.textContent = navigator.globalPrivacyControl === true
        ? "Analytics is off: your browser sends Global Privacy Control."
        : off ? "Analytics is off on this browser." : "Analytics is on.";
    }
    button.addEventListener("click", function () {
      try {
        if (read()) localStorage.removeItem("ltg-analytics");
        else localStorage.setItem("ltg-analytics", "off");
      } catch (e) {
        state.textContent = "Your browser is blocking site storage, so this setting can't be saved. Block cookies in your browser instead.";
        return;
      }
      show();
    });
    show();
  })();
</script>

<style>
  .legal {
    max-width: 52rem;
    padding-block: var(--space-7);
  }

  .legal h1 {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }

  .legal__intro {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 1.15rem;
  }

  .legal h2 {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.55rem, 4vw, 2.25rem);
  }

  .legal p,
  .legal ul {
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .legal li + li {
    margin-top: 0.4rem;
  }

  .legal a {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 750;
  }

  .legal__switch {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.75rem 1rem;
  }

  .legal__button {
    padding: 0.6rem 1.1rem;
    border: 0;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--chrome);
    color: var(--chrome-text);
    font: inherit;
    font-weight: 700;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .legal__button:hover,
  .legal__button:focus-visible {
    background: var(--accent);
    color: var(--surface);
  }
</style>
